   "hypothesis": "Hypothesis: additive composition under the output sigmoid, logit = 2.58 + Linear + 5.14*Ramp + 1.53*A5not4 + 0.105*A6. a4:2, a4:3, a5:3 have no enabled connections (zero-effect entries). The model is an upper-edge-only count detector: for a1 in {1,2} it is positive while few attributes take their first value and negative once about three of {a2,a3,a4,a6} (a1=1) or four (a1=2) do; a5=1 counts only through Linear's -14.8, which is not enough to flip a1=1 inputs with one other first value. There is no lower edge: inputs with zero or one first value get the largest logits. a1=3 inputs are all positive (107/107 on train) via Linear's +24.9. Evidence (train, n=345): positive rate by (a1, count) - a1=1: count<=2 100%, 3 74%, >=4 0%; a1=2: count<=3 100%, 4 29%, 5 0%; a1=3: 100% at every count. Predicts positive on 85.5% of train rows (accuracy 0.472 at 0.5). Logits reach |~130| so the sigmoid saturates; the sigmoid-output AUC 0.807 is inflated by ties at 1.0, the logit ranking AUC is 0.734. Compared with the MONK-2 target (exactly two first values): the network captures only the upper edge (>=3-4 first values -> negative) and none of the lower edge (0-1 -> negative), and ignores the count entirely when a1=3.",
